$Id: README.gui,v 1.2 2011/05/16 00:23:26 drmiller Exp $

The GUI is java based. All the *.class files are required, and optional fonts
are desirable. All fonts are *.ttf and in the "fonts" subdirectory.

This does seem to build and run correctly on OSX as well as Linux (known only on Debian).

Basic build procesdure is "make". This also attempts to install the font(s) in
a subdirectory in your home directory.

The Wang 600 GUI is started with the command:

	java w600_fe

This creates a sub-process to run the simulator. Currently, you still need
the terminal window for the printer, and for any diagnostic output.
